const description = 'A research-based look at the Grundig S08 heavy-duty tire pressure monitoring system, including 8–12-wheel configurations, pressure limits, alarm setup, and cold-weather checks.';
const image = 'https://grundig-auto.com/cdn/shop/files/S08-8-wheel-version.webp';
const affiliate = 'https://www.awin1.com/cread.php?awinmid=130595&awinaffid=3119041&ued=https%3A%2F%2Fgrundig-auto.com%2Fproducts%2Fgrundig-s08-rv-tpms';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image={image}>
<article class="s08-article">
  <p class="s08-kicker">THE PRACTICAL EDIT / RV &amp; AUTOMOTIVE</p>
  <header class="s08-hero">
    <div class="s08-hero-copy">
      <p class="s08-kicker">COLD-SEASON CHECKLIST</p>
      <h1>The first cold snap: setting up a heavy-duty TPMS before winter</h1>
      <p class="s08-deck">For larger motorhomes, heavy fifth wheels and multi-axle towing setups, a tire pressure monitoring system can add an in-cab view of pressure and temperature across more wheels.</p>
      <a class="s08-button" href={affiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer">Check Price ↗</a>
      <p class="s08-disclaimer">Affiliate link. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. This is a research-based product overview, not a hands-on test.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="s08-hero-image" href={affiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View the Grundig S08 heavy-duty TPMS">
      <img src={image} alt="Grundig S08 heavy-duty tire pressure monitoring system" fetchpriority="high" />
    </a>
  </header>

  <p class="s08-intro">A drop in outdoor temperature is a useful prompt to check tire pressures before a long drive. Larger RVs and towing combinations can have many tires to inspect, and the correct pressure depends on the vehicle, tire, load and setup. The Grundig S08 is designed for larger configurations, with selectable wheel modes and a display intended to keep pressure readings and alerts visible from the cab.</p>

  <div class="s08-facts">
    <div><span>Designed for</span><strong>8–12-wheel setups*</strong></div>
    <div><span>Listed maximum range</span><strong>Up to 217 PSI*</strong></div>
    <div><span>Display</span><strong>5-inch HD</strong></div>
    <div><span>Advertised starting price</span><strong>$259*</strong></div>
  </div>
  <p class="s08-footnote">*Specifications and pricing may vary by selected sensor kit and can change. Confirm the exact configuration and current listing before ordering. The product page lists several sensor combinations and both standard-pressure and heavy-duty options.</p>

  <h2>What the S08 is designed to do</h2>
  <p>Grundig lists the S08 for 8-, 10- and 12-wheel configurations, with supported pressure capacity up to 217 PSI when paired with the appropriate high-pressure sensors. Its 5-inch display is designed to show tire information and alerts, while the system's stated wireless range is up to 40 meters in suitable conditions. Actual signal performance can vary with vehicle construction, placement and distance.</p>

  <div class="s08-feature-grid">
    <section><span class="s08-number">01</span><h3>More wheel positions</h3><p>The selectable configuration can suit some Class A motorhomes, heavy fifth wheels, toy haulers and commercial-style setups. Confirm the wheel count and sensor mix before buying.</p></section>
    <section><span class="s08-number">02</span><h3>High-pressure sensor options</h3><p>The product listing offers sensor variants for different pressure requirements. The maximum system range is not a recommendation for your tire inflation pressure.</p></section>
    <section><span class="s08-number">03</span><h3>Receiver with a built-in battery</h3><p>The manufacturer lists a 650 mAh monitor battery and USB charging. Keep the display charged and check the manual for operation and pairing steps.</p></section>
  </div>

  <h2>The most important step: set the alarms for your rig</h2>
  <p>Do not assume the factory alarm thresholds match your vehicle. Grundig's listing gives default low- and high-pressure alarms of 72 PSI and 145 PSI, respectively, while the supported monitoring range can extend higher with the appropriate sensors. Those defaults may not be right for your particular tires and load.</p>
  <p>Use the vehicle placard, tire manufacturer's guidance and the correct load/inflation information to determine the required cold inflation pressures and appropriate alert settings. Do not set pressure targets based only on the maximum PSI printed on a tire sidewall, and never change tire pressure simply to silence an alarm. Follow the vehicle, tire and TPMS instructions.</p>

  <aside class="s08-note"><strong>Before your first winter trip:</strong> Confirm the correct sensor kit, configure the wheel count, adjust alert thresholds according to the manufacturer's guidance, pair and verify each sensor position, and make sure the receiver is charged before departure.</aside>

  <h2>Cold-weather checks still matter</h2>
  <p>Check tire pressures when the tires are cold, inspect tread and sidewalls for visible damage, and make sure tires are appropriate for the vehicle's load. Verify that the monitor reports each sensor and that the displayed wheel positions make sense. A TPMS can help flag pressure or temperature changes, but it cannot identify every tire problem or replace a calibrated pressure gauge and regular inspection.</p>

  <h2>Who should consider the S08?</h2>
  <p>The S08 may be worth considering if your compatible RV or towing setup needs to monitor more than six wheels, or if its pressure range and sensor options match your requirements. It may be more system than a smaller camper or a six-wheel dually needs. For a fixed six-wheel setup, compare the more focused S04 option before deciding.</p>

  <div class="s08-product-card">
    <img src={image} alt="Grundig S08 heavy-duty TPMS display and sensor kit" loading="lazy" />
    <div><p class="s08-kicker">THE PRODUCT AT A GLANCE</p><h2>Grundig S08 Heavy-Duty TPMS</h2><p>A multi-wheel monitoring system with a 5-inch display and selectable sensor kits. Check the listing carefully for pressure rating, wheel count, sensor type, booster options and current price.</p><a class="s08-button" href={affiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer">Check Price at Grundig Auto ↗</a><p class="s08-small">Prices, availability and included components can change on the advertiser's site.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Our Buy Better Finds take</h2>
  <p>The S08's main draw is its combination of multi-wheel support and high-pressure sensor options. The right choice depends on the number of tires you need to monitor, the actual pressure requirements, and which sensor kit fits your setup—not just the headline maximum PSI.</p>
  <p>We have not personally tested this system. This overview is based on the manufacturer's published product information, so confirm the latest specifications, compatibility and setup instructions before purchase.</p>
  <p class="s08-related"><strong>Comparing configurations?</strong> Read our <a href="/blog/grundig-s04-six-wheel-tpms-cold-season/">Grundig S04 six-wheel TPMS guide</a> if you have a six-wheel setup, or use the manufacturer's listing to confirm which model and sensor kit suit your vehicle.</p>
  <a class="s08-button" href={affiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer">Check Current Price ↗</a>
